  "commemorated_topic": "25th anniversary of accession of Queen Elizabeth II",
  "comments": "<p>The second crown-sized coin to be issued following Decimalisation Day on 15th February 1971, the denomination was updated from 5 shillings to 25 new pence. Despite being produced in their millions and being available at face value from most post offices and banks, the ordinary business strike was a Royal Mint commemorative issue and not intended for general circulation.<br><br>In addition to the circulation standard issue, there was also a BU strike in a presentation folder and a proof strike was issued as part of the Annual Proof coin set.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/628151e4a5fe9.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/628151e4a5fe9.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/68050c04487eb.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/68050c04487eb.jpg\"></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/68050c03d7ecd.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/68050c03d7ecd.jpg\"></a><br><br>(former Spink ref. 4227)</p>",
